---
title: Experimental setup schematic
---

A figure component whose source is executable code rather than a binary blob.
Rendering this document to an image produces a panel that figmint can insert,
and `--credentials` attaches a signed C2PA manifest recording that Stencila
produced it:

```sh
stencila render schematic.smd schematic.png --credentials --yes
```

The resulting PNG carries an `org.stencila.provenance` assertion — a JSON-LD
graph naming the producing software and the pre-signing content digest. figmint
reads that during its directory scan, so the panel arrives already knowing where
it came from, with no sidecar needed.

```graphviz exec
digraph setup {
  rankdir=LR;
  node [shape=box, style=rounded, fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=10];
  edge [fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=9];

  inlet   [label="Inlet\ntank"];
  pump    [label="Pump"];
  section [label="Test\nsection", style="rounded,filled", fillcolor="#e5eefd"];
  turbine [label="Turbine", style="rounded,filled", fillcolor="#efe6fb"];
  daq     [label="DAQ", shape=box3d];

  inlet -> pump [label="  flow"];
  pump -> section;
  section -> turbine [label="  U∞"];
  turbine -> daq [label="  torque,\n  RPM", style=dashed];
}
```
